================================================================================
RESERVED INVENTIONS AND DESIGNS
================================================================================

The following architectural innovations and designs disclosed in the Work are
the original creations of the Author and are reserved without limitation. This
list is non-exhaustive; the Author's reservation of rights extends to all novel
contributions whether or not enumerated here.

  - Content-addressed substrate combining cross-source Glicko-2 consensus,
    geometric placement on a closed 4-ball coordinate space, and per-arena
    attestation accumulation across multi-source ingestion

  - Per-vertex semantic encoding via mantissa packing of float64 IEEE 754
    representations to carry content-addressed identity, ordinal position,
    run-length compression, and per-vertex metadata simultaneously in a single
    PostGIS geometry column

  - Recipe-driven substrate synthesis for arbitrary user-authored AI model
    target architectures, including per-layer arena cognitive function
    decomposition, substrate-derived layer normalization parameters, substrate-
    derived position embeddings, FFN-as-edge-slot synthesis, attention
    reconstruction via E·M·E^T = S least-squares with sign discrimination,
    and embedding synthesis via Belkin & Niyogi 2003 Laplacian eigenmap of
    substrate adjacency

  - The Substrate Synthesis SaaS product surface — customer-authored recipe
    configuration including hardware-target-aware feasibility envelopes,
    deterministic pre-flight pricing via recipe-cost estimation, opt-in
    cross-customer content sharing with per-attestation revenue share, and
    conversational mode powered by substrate-native AI agents

  - The Gödel engine three-scale OODA loop on substrate (Micro per-traversal-
    step annotation, Meso per-query Observe-Orient-Decide-Act with Reflexion
    retry and Self-Consistency voting, Macro background frayed-edge survey and
    curiosity-driven gap-prediction)

  - Cross-model consensus surface via firefly POINTZM physicalities, with
    Voronoi-tessellation centroid + dispersion + agreement scoring, and
    pairwise cross-model divergence measurement

  - Tree-sitter grammar bidirectional content codec wherein Tree-sitter
    grammars serve as both parsers and generators for any formally-specified
    structural domain, with substrate accumulating cross-grammar attested
    patterns to drive grammar-conformant generation of arbitrary structured
    content

  - The substrate-as-Merkle-DAG-as-AST unification, wherein the substrate's
    typed-composition structure is structurally identical to the abstract
    syntax tree representation Tree-sitter and similar parsing systems produce

  - The architectural insight that the substrate is the universal infrastructure
    for all formally-structured digital knowledge, replacing rather than
    competing with AI training systems, knowledge graphs, vector databases,
    model deployment platforms, custom-tuning SaaS, mechanistic interpretability
    research tooling, AI auditing infrastructure, and domain-specific knowledge
    engines

  - The anti-pattern numbering discipline (AP-N), the substrate's law-based
    architectural constraint system, and the vocabulary-as-architecture-
    discipline doctrine

  - The cross-mechanism consensus principle whereby embedding cosine, attention
    pair-score, and FFN co-activation independently attest the same substrate
    edge identity, accumulating per-arena Glicko-weighted consensus across
    mechanisms and across models

  - The three-tier data model (seed / app / user) with arena-scoped privacy,
    asymptotic per-customer cost reduction via content-addressed cross-customer
    deduplication, and the customer-content marketplace mechanism

  - The substrate as scientific instrument — empirical apparatus for the
    Finite Universe Theorem cardinality measurement, the Lottery Ticket
    Hypothesis (substrate variant) validation, and Mendeleev-aspect
    gap-prediction via void detection

Independent recreation, reimplementation, or imitation of these inventions
does not transfer rights to the imitator. Prior art assertions challenging
the Author's claims of original invention are addressed on the merits; the
Author reserves all rights to pursue assertion of original authorship.

